                        "entry_id": "3598bdc6-3c74-3334-a675-cccc9e05a078",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Enough to fill a skin."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3958634e-0775-4ec3-aa29-90d2f003f919",
                                "sense_id": "408e4cc7-cb5c-3ba0-8cdd-0267ddbcf51c",
                                "text": "a skinful of wine"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5c590e03-5990-303d-934a-b792d3d1bc95",
                        "entry_id": "3598bdc6-3c74-3334-a675-cccc9e05a078",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Enough alcoholic drink to cause inebriation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d41dcc8c-d7d2-427c-9e78-999dc5a0a8de",
                                "sense_id": "5c590e03-5990-303d-934a-b792d3d1bc95",
                                "text": "I wasn't thinking straight – I'd had a skinful that night."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4b8d1df8-cd8a-4b7a-8f25-5f001a452866",
                                "sense_id": "5c590e03-5990-303d-934a-b792d3d1bc95",
                                "text": "When methodist preachers come down,\nA-preaching that drinking is sinful,\nI'll wager the rascals a crown,\nThey always preach best with a skinful."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "af815b02-bad2-4b84-8e6d-d3e391ac223c",
                                "sense_id": "5c590e03-5990-303d-934a-b792d3d1bc95",
                                "text": "“’E generally goes down there when ’e’s got ’is skinful, beggin’ your pardon, sir, an’ they do say that the more lush — in-he-briated ’e is, the more fish ’e catches.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dc088649-2c57-46ff-9b39-2c7e4e22d48b",
                                "sense_id": "5c590e03-5990-303d-934a-b792d3d1bc95",
                                "text": "\"People who've had a skinful,\" Robey explains. \"They lose their inhibitions and forget the boundaries of acceptable behaviour."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "25ae070a-3876-38aa-aac1-e6e5bece5e5a",
                        "entry_id": "3598bdc6-3c74-3334-a675-cccc9e05a078",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Plenty; a large amount."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "674af996-969e-4fd0-a02e-90cae8e6ccc3",
                                "sense_id": "25ae070a-3876-38aa-aac1-e6e5bece5e5a",
                                "text": "To steal a housewife's purse might mean that her children would have to go hungry; but what of that, if the flash young “dip” could gain admiration from his mates by boasting that he had “frisked a judy's cly and lifted a skinful of bunce”?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "147b59cd-638c-4ae4-95cc-310604e392b3",
                                "sense_id": "25ae070a-3876-38aa-aac1-e6e5bece5e5a",
                                "text": "“Now there's a skinful of abuse!” the curly top exclaimed. “Sounds as if she crossed the ocean just to denounce you in a public place.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
